/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-23-  rule seqLen(tuple(VS:ValSeq))                 => vsLen(VS)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-24-  rule seqLen(str(IS:IntSeq))                   => isLen(IS)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-25-  rule seqLen(setV(DS:IntSeq))                  => isLen(DS)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k:26:  rule seqLen(rangeObj(LO:Int, HI:Int, ST:Int)) => rangeLen(LO, HI, ST)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-27-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-28-  // ==== list(seq) — materialize a list/tuple into a list (e.g. list(d.keys())) ==
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-29-  // Minimal: the "copy a sequence" case (list of a list is itself; list of a tuple keeps order).
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k:30:  // list() of other iterables (str/range/set/zip) is added via the iterator fold when needed.
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-31-  // (k-cell — list() constructs a NEW object)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-32-  rule <k> #applyK(toCall(builtinV("list")), (list(VS:ValSeq),  .Vals)) => #alloc(list(VS)) ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-33-  rule <k> #applyK(toCall(builtinV("list")), (tuple(VS:ValSeq), .Vals)) => #alloc(list(VS)) ... </k>
