/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/list.k-21-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/list.k-22-  // list + list constructs a NEW object (k-cell — it allocates; operands land here
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/list.k-23-  // already deref'd). priority(45) beats the generic BinOp dispatch.
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/list.k:24:  rule <k> BinOp("+", list(A:ValSeq), list(B:ValSeq)) => #alloc(list(valSeqConcat(A, B))) ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/list.k-25-       [priority(45)]
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/list.k-26-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/list.k-27-  rule applyCmp("==", list(A:ValSeq), list(B:ValSeq)) => A ==K B
